{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The U-Net architecture is the gold standard for semantic image segmentation, consisting of a contracting path (encoder) to capture context and a symmetric expanding path (decoder) for precise spatial localization, linked via skip connections."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Input Image ──► [ DoubleConv ] ────────────────────── Skip ─────────────────────► [ Up + Conv ] ──► Mask","                     │                                                                ▲","                  [ Down ] ──► [ DoubleConv ] ──────── Skip ───────► [ Up + Conv ] ───┘","                                   │                                     ▲","                                [ Down ] ──► [ Bottleneck Conv ] ────────┘"]},{"anchor":"1-Initializing-and-Running-U-Net","type":"heading","text":"1. Initializing and Running U-Net","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftVision","","\/\/ Initialize U-Net on Apple Silicon Metal GPU","let unet = UNetArchitecture(inChannels: 3, outChannels: 1, baseFeatures: 32)","","\/\/ Forward pass on image tensor (Batch x Height x Width x Channels)","let imageTensor = try ImageTensorLoader.load(url: URL(fileURLWithPath: \"sample.jpg\"))","let maskOutput = try unet.forward(image: imageTensor)","","print(\"Output mask dimensions: \\(maskOutput.shape)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Vision-Network-Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetDoubleConv","doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetDown","doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetUp","doc:\/\/SwiftVision\/documentation\/SwiftVision\/UNetOutConv"],"title":"Vision Network Types"}],"identifier":{"ur